OL,3,GNEWSABalaclava bans: Will they actually
OL,4,Awork?
OL,5,
OL,6,FFor some, a balaclava is about privacy,
OL,7,Fcomfort or keeping warm.
OL,9,FFor others, it has become a symbol of
OL,10,Fanti-social behaviour, intimidation and
OL,11,Fcrime.
OL,13,FThat divide is at the heart of new
OL,14,Fpowers being introduced in Stafford,
OL,15,Fwhere people can be ordered to remove
OL,16,Fface coverings if officers believe they
OL,17,Fare being used to conceal someone's
OL,18,Fidentity while committing crime or
OL,19,Fcausing anti-social behaviour.
OL,23,APub: 20-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
